      "widgets_values": [
        "One clear photo per character. Head-and-shoulders or half-body reads best;\na tiny face in a wide shot has few reference tokens to give.\n\nBoth faces are placed in a SINGLE pass. Chaining two single-character edits\nis less reliable - the second pass tends to re-render the first face.\n\nThe B slot is the LoRA's 'subject' slot and pulls harder on the output.\nThat asymmetry is why identity_a usually ends up ABOVE identity_b.\n\nWire the same images, in the same order, into the encode node."
      ],
      "title": "Two people, one pass",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
